"""Deterministic documentation from independent manifests and explicit gate log.

The gate log is evidence for documentation only. It never participates in Model
or Expected derivation. No target/Actual report is read by this renderer.
"""
import json

PREFIX="phase-04c1b4a-"


def table(header,rows):
    return "| "+" | ".join(header)+" |\n| "+" | ".join("---" for _ in header)+" |\n"+"\n".join("| "+" | ".join(str(item).replace("|","\\|") for item in row)+" |" for row in rows)+"\n"


def documents(coverage,manifest,mutation_manifest,hand,pending,evidence):
    types=coverage["type_level"];projection=coverage["projection_type_level"];cases=manifest["cases"]
    totals=manifest["instance_totals"]
    closed=evidence.get("all_gates")=="passed"
    outcome="Outcome A — D9 Control Oracle Subset Closed" if closed else "Verification in progress; no closure claim"
    counts=table(["Count family","Value"],list(types.items())+list(projection.items()))
    case_table=table(["CaseId","Stage","Required instances","Diagnostic instances"],[(case["case_id"],case["expected_stage"],case["instance_coverage"]["required"],case["instance_coverage"]["diagnostic"]) for case in cases])
    provenance={name:sum(case["oracle_provenance"][name] for case in cases) for name in ["IndependentAlgebra","ExactDeclarations","ContentIdentity","DiagnosticOnly"]}
    common=f"\nScope: the 22 existing D9-Control CaseIds only. D10 independent value comparison remains Pending. Historical CaseIds and Expected are unchanged. Starting HEAD: `5aa4ef7b865b9255a29c83c8375e13803d5e5ce1`.\n"
    docs={}
    docs["overview"]=f"# Phase 4C.1B.4A\n\n{outcome}.\n{common}\nThe executable field contract is a finite grammar plus a frozen source type graph. Independent Expected comes from Portable declarations, exact content identities and Python control algebra. Both sides validate against the grammar before all required values compare. The test-build projection adds recursive fields omitted by the old diagnostic view without changing production semantics.\n\nThe registered subset contains all thirteen Opcode kinds and nine additional control trees. Core proof/context/container members are getter-bound; unused typed payloads and all D10 value proofs remain in the exact Pending inventories. This does not close B01/B02 or authorize a later phase.\n\n"+counts
    inventory=table(["Rust field path","Full type","Classification","Applicable cases","Projection binding"],[(field["typed_field_path"],"`"+field["full_type"]+"`",field["classification"],len(field["case_applicability"]),", ".join(field["projection_bindings"]) or "Pending") for field in coverage["fields"]])
    nominal=table(["Nominal terminal","Underlying type","Namespace","Source"],[(name,item["scalar_type"],item["namespace"],item["source"]) for name,item in coverage["rust_type_graph"]["nominal_scalar_definitions"].items()])
    docs["type-field-inventory"]="# Complete finite type/field inventory\n"+common+"\nThe inventory has "+str(len(coverage["rust_type_graph"]["types"]))+" reachable Rust record/sum types and six separately registered macro-defined nominal scalar terminals. Generic and recursive edges are type references, not infinitely expanded paths. Struct members, every enum tag/payload, Option presence and collection element types are inventoried from declarations. The source inventory and normalized semantic projection counts are separate domains; a source member can bind to multiple projection slots. Container/data identities are compared in their declared canonical semantic view, not pointer addresses or internal hash-map layout. Unused payload branches remain Pending.\n\n"+counts+"\n## Nominal scalar terminals\n\n"+nominal+"\n## Every Rust member/variant slot\n\n"+inventory+"\n## Every normalized projection field\n\n"+table(["Projection type path","Stage","Class","Applicable cases","Status"],[(f["field_path"],f["stage"],f["classification"],len(f["case_applicability"]),f["oracle_status"]) for f in coverage["projection_fields"]])
    docs["executable-coverage-contract"]="# Executable field contract\n"+common+"\n`coverage/field-coverage.json` registers finite record/union/ref/array/tuple/nullable/scalar schemas. Every key is required; a nullable field still requires its key and explicit null. Every collection has an element schema. Nominal coordinates are U32, occurrence/Usage/count values U64, time/Int64 values I64, relation byte elements U8. Fixed TIMEOUT outcomes have arity two and D10 has nine unique dimension identities.\n\nExpected shape and Actual shape validate independently. Both-side deletion of `Node.operator` fails before equality. Both-side insertion of an unregistered member also fails. Checked ownership relates direct child order to recursively emitted child identities; leaf kind/node/caller identity must agree. A new production type member fails the frozen declaration comparison until an explicit inventory review and getter binding occur. Mandatory D9 core records cannot have an unbound member.\n\nProof arrays and inherited obligations compare as canonical multisets: duplicate members remain, all source/verdict/rule/reference/prerequisite values compare, and only free explanation prose is omitted. All other arrays preserve formal order. The finite grammar counts a required container/variant/presence slot and every instantiated payload visit; references and union dispatch do not add visits. An Option's presence and Some payload are separately typed visits. These counts are reproducible, not counts of printed JSON keys.\n\nDiagnostic exclusions are only `ControlDimensionProof.reason`, `LeafDimensionProof.reason`, `DimensionProof.reason`, `InheritedControlObligation.reason`, and `ActionGuardCompatibility.reason`: unconstrained human explanations have no nominal identity. Their presence and string type still validate. Enum lower-bound adjustment reasons, RuleIds, references, prerequisites, source coordinates and countermodels remain required.\n"
    operators=[("INVOKE","exact checked declaration and call-site mappings","AF-SEMANTIC-0111..0117"),("AWAIT","unknown adapter dimensions; exact signal/correlation and external provenance","AF-SEMANTIC-0122"),("CALL_SUBFLOW","exact target/export association; body RequiresEvidence","AF-SEMANTIC-0118..0121"),("SEQUENCE","ordered accumulation; later positive effect lowers weaken","AF-SEMANTIC-0127"),("SELECT","exclusive join; checked constant case; other source facts retained","AF-SEMANTIC-0128/0129"),("PARALLEL","all branch uppers; fail-fast weakens lowers; no inflight multiplier","AF-SEMANTIC-0130/0131"),("RACE","loser effects, Usage and K/X sources retained; no winner","AF-SEMANTIC-0132/0133"),("ITERATE","[0,n] effect repetition and one Usage multiplier","AF-SEMANTIC-0143"),("RETRY","logical multiplier once; physical attempts separately projected","AF-SEMANTIC-0144"),("TIMEOUT","child facts retained; two control outcomes outside Phi","AF-SEMANTIC-0145"),("HANDLE","exact residual Phi; protected + conditional exclusive handlers","AF-SEMANTIC-0146"),("SCOPE","exact lexical resources; absent authority/budget Unproven; settlement RequiresEvidence","AF-SEMANTIC-0147/0148"),("COMPENSATION_SCOPE","forward facts retained; empty closed action multiset, exact local scope","AF-SEMANTIC-0149..0151")]
    docs["d9-control-oracle"]="# Independent D9 control model\n"+common+"\n`d9_control_model.py` resolves exact declared Bundle assets and caller/source associations; `d9_algebra.py` performs independent E/Phi/U calculations; `field_contract.py` validates typed semantic projections. No Rust checker, FFI, Actual file or runtime report is an Expected input. Existing Python ACE1/HashV1 and declaration recapture helpers are reused. CaseId binds the resulting value to its immutable input checksum; it does not select a canned report.\n\n"+table(["Opcode","Independent rule","Normative attribution"],operators)+"\nEvery node retains recursive children, leaf facts, interface, scope, all seven dimension values and their proofs, occurrences/residuals, aliases, adjustments, sequence dataflow, inherited obligations and same-context association. Root retains closure, resolver identity, all dimensions and full Recovery fields. Proof references use the registered internal coordinate vocabulary (computation token, pinned digest or exact schema identity). Fresh checked inputs discharge static input premises; this closed report profile declares no extra prerequisite-string instances. Remaining unknown/evidence obligations stay in typed verdict/availability/source fields; the prerequisites collection is still mandatory and compared exactly.\n\nOutside this subset, active K actions, nonempty public output expansion, nonempty subflow interface/dependency expansion and incomplete child E/Phi/U require a separate model and raise OracleGap. They are not emptied or skipped. FOREACH finite/dynamic E/U algebra exists, while uninstantiated binding/payload branches remain inventoried Pending.\n"
    docs["d9-effect-failure-usage"]="# Independent E, Phi and U\n"+common+"\nEffect identities include operation, every qualifier member, selector port/scope, guard and bounds. Accumulation uses checked sums; SELECT joins/maxes with frozen guard/lower rules; SEQUENCE later lowers and RACE/fail-fast lowers weaken without erasing uppers. HANDLE adds protected work to the exclusive/no-handler envelope. ITERATE and RETRY multiply once with their distinct lower/count semantics; TIMEOUT retains work. Residual and Unknown states have separate tags.\n\nPhi is an exact nominal TypeSchemaRef union, with exact HANDLE removal plus possible handler failures. Timeout, cancellation, race winner and RecoveryBlocked are not inserted into business Phi. Leaf/node identity and recursive paths retain failure provenance.\n\nUsage is keyed by phase and complete meter identity; units/aggregation remain in the exact context recapture. Missing coordinates become Unknown under composition, distinct from explicit zero and known unbounded. Handler no-handler zeroes exist only at explicitly declared coordinates. Python integers are checked as exact U64 values; floats/bools/noncanonical numerals and overflow fail. Runtime reservations, costs and refunds are absent.\n"
    docs["d9-resource-flow-execution"]="# Independent R, F and X\n"+common+"\nR derives full requirements, public resource type pins, caller slots, exact mapping evidence and aliases. Same numeric port values at different call sites retain source namespaces; alias grouping never reduces E/U. Scope resource visibility is computed from owned lexical edges and exact declared resources.\n\nF retains source/sink coordinates, labels, taints, may-carry instruction authority and partitions. Known summaries merge conservatively; race/retry/timeout/iterate/handler decisions stay unknown. A Partial child remains a distinct unresolved source even when its known subtotal's list is empty. Selector/control value dependencies remain explicit. AWAIT stays external/unknown and does not acquire trusted authority. Action-specific F remains outside this source model.\n\nX retains every child's complete exact requirements independently: capability/version, sandbox, trust, region/residency, runtime profile, ABI and preferences. Concurrent work is not assigned one worker. D9 carries constraints; D10's separate feasibility/security verdicts are inventoried Pending as independent value proofs.\n"
    docs["d9-source-closure"]="# Source and closure derivation\n"+common+"\nThe Oracle computes owned preorder and leaf preorder from the declared IR child edges, validates unique identities and accounts for every declared node. Exact resolver associations select declared checked assets by full pins. HashV1 is recomputed over each used contract/IR asset, schema content pins are independently checked, and relation plain SHA-256 checksums are recomputed. Same contract at two nodes yields two source instances.\n\nClosure preserves all known occurrences, residuals and K sources; it is separate from root export compatibility. The latter stays NotExpressedInSemanticIr/Unproven. Context content is recaptured from declarations and compared with getter-based D5 recapture, while every D9 leaf/node must share its root's freshly rebuilt arena. No process pointer address is an identity.\n\nThe 22-case sources have no active K action. The Oracle checks this exact declared binding multiset before emitting an empty action/effect/Usage fold. AWAIT has no adapter K source and keeps Unknown with its source id. CompensationScope retains nearest local scope and forward facts; no action owner, count or usage profile is invented. The specialized 16-case nonempty K model remains Pending.\n"
    docs["full-field-differential"]="# Full-field D9 differential\n"+common+"\nBoth implementations validate the closed schema, then compare every required typed visit. The Rust projection extension is under cfg(test); production serializers and checker behavior are unchanged. The data is analysis evidence, with no Checked constructor or serialization. Full child facts and dimension proof arrays are added using typed getters.\n\n"+case_table+"\n"+table(["Aggregate","Count"],[("Expected required",totals["required"]),("Expected diagnostic",totals["diagnostic"]),("Declared existing CaseIds",22)])+"\nThe exact executed/compared/missing/unexpected counts are recorded in the gate evidence. D10 shape validation is separate and its independent values remain Pending.\n\n"+table(["Oracle origin family","Instantiated visits"],provenance.items())+"\nOrigin accounting uses deterministic path families: complete context/pin/checksum identities, exact leaf declarations/source ids, and derived control/closure/proof facts. Diagnostic prose is counted separately.\n"
    docs["comparator-mutations"]="# Independent comparator mutations\n"+common+"\nThe previous 68 Actual-baseline self-tests are retained as comparator integrity evidence. This phase adds "+str(mutation_manifest["mutation_count"])+" mutations whose baselines are independent frozen Expected; 32 use original Control sidecars and 10 use independently generated rich input-mutation expectations. One semantic field changes per mutation. Each must fail typed shape/relations or exact comparison and report its deep path. Both-side omission and unregistered additions are also tested.\n\n"+table(["Mutation","Expected source","Typed path"],[(row["mutation_id"],row.get("case_slug",row.get("expected_file")),".".join(row["path"])) for row in mutation_manifest["mutations"]])
    docs["hand-calculation"]="# Hand-derived cross-checks\n"+common+"\nThese literal expected values were derived from the formal rules, without Rust output. The ten control-algebra operators plus INVOKE/AWAIT/CALL_SUBFLOW cover all thirteen opcodes. Additional vectors check exact HANDLE residual Phi, missing versus zero Usage, U64 overflow, Retry x Iterate, Sequence + Retry, Select + Handle, Parallel + Race and Iterate + CompensationScope. Inputs, intermediate factors and expected results are preserved below.\n\n"+"\n".join("## "+row["vector_id"]+"\n\n```json\n"+json.dumps(row,indent=2)+"\n```\n" for row in hand["vectors"])
    docs["remaining-coverage"]="# Exact remaining coverage\n"+common+"\n"+counts+"\nThe 22 original cases close only their applicable D9 fields. The other 56 historical CaseIds are not promoted; D10 independent proof values remain Pending for all 78. Source backing types/uninstantiated payloads and D10 members are individually listed, not hidden as diagnostics.\n\n4C.1B.4B requires the 16 specialized Recovery cases: exact local/root action bounds, owner paths, unique factors, source/action/profile multisets, same-atom E/K coverage, action guards/countermodels and complete Usage profiles. Later C/D work requires complete assertion/context/compiler/resolver content identities, all typed mappings, preflight and nine-dimension proof/witness/obligation/value models, followed by six-scenario cross-process full-field comparison. Those phases are not started.\n\n## Other historical CaseIds\n\n"+"\n".join("- `"+case+"`" for case in pending["other_case_ids"])+"\n\n## Pending source members\n\n"+"\n".join("- `"+path+"`" for path in pending["source_fields"])+"\n\n## Pending projection members\n\n"+"\n".join("- `"+path+"`" for path in pending["projection_fields"])+"\n"
    docs["readiness"]=f"# Readiness\n\n{outcome}.\n{common}\nOnly a successful committed implementation gate permits the 4C.1B.4A subset-complete claim. Full D9/D10 conformance remains incomplete. B01/B02 implementation remains present and conformance closure BLOCKING; B03-B07 remain BLOCKING. Independent Portable Proof Integration Audit is not started. F01/F02 remain CLOSED, F03/F04 OPEN/P2; no production soundness finding is confirmed by these agreeing cases.\n\n4C.1B.4B admission: {'ready after this subset gate, but not executed' if closed else 'pending final gates'}. No later phase, runtime or publication capability is created.\n"
    docs["gate-report"]="# Gate report\n"+common+"\nThis evidence log is used only for documentation, never for Expected generation. Normal generation checks the frozen source graph before deriving values. The full static surface and historical Expected remain anchored to the starting HEAD.\n\n```json\n"+json.dumps(evidence,indent=2)+"\n```\n\nAll current generators must run twice and produce identical bytes. Full workspace gates use build parallelism two on Windows. Cargo regression success does not close the still-Pending D10/Recovery proof models.\n"
    return {PREFIX+name+".md":text for name,text in docs.items()}
